      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>I have an intersting relationship with that set, I consider the villains and enviroments to be punishingly tough, but in terms of flavor I love the set and I dont know what the artist would think but I consider the best set in terms of artistic experimentation. There are several nods to Frank Miller in the art, Mr. Fixer has those cool &quot;style&quot; cards and every card back has a lot of flavor, like the tabloid cover for Plague Rat or the dossier on Spite.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>As for Spite he is a real challenge that requires a lot of teamwork and control, and his whole victim angle is really interesting.</p>",
